## State coverage (every branch the web source carries renders; no hidden surfaces)
visibility: hidden (opacity-0 scale-95) <-> revealed (opacity-100 scale-100); pointer hover
            (onHover) OR tap (web :focus-within for touch)                  [web group-hover/focus-within]
placement:  top | bottom | left(leading) | right(trailing)                 [web sideClasses]
wrap:       single-line (whitespace-nowrap) | multiline (max-w-[260px])     [web multiline]
surface:    inverted high-contrast card (bg=textPrimary / fg=bg tokens) +
            increased-contrast hairline                                     [web dark: invert + forced-colors:border]
motion:     reveal disabled under Reduce Motion                            [web motion-reduce:transition-none]
empty:      empty / whitespace body -> NO floating box (never a blank box) + no view.opened
note: data-lifecycle states (loading/error/stale/offline) are NOT branches of this
      presentational primitive — the web source's only hook is `useId` (no fetch, no cache,
      no promise). They belong to the embedding FEATURE surface that supplies the content,
      the same faithful-parity ownership split the sibling HelpTooltip (0216) documents and
      the prior 0231 run recorded. The one lifecycle peer this surface owns — "empty" — is
      implemented + tested (TooltipProjector.shouldRenderBubble / hasContent).

